$NetBSD$

The paxctl call the BSD port adds is a recipe line, but it is indented
with spaces while every other recipe line in this macro uses a tab.  It
is reached only when OPENJDK_TARGET_OS_ENV is bsd.netbsd, so only a
NetBSD build sees it, and what it sees is

  gensrc/GensrcAdlc.gmk:75: *** missing separator (did you mean TAB
  instead of 8 spaces?).  Stop.

named against the eval that expanded the macro, not against this line, so
which file is blamed depends on which link the build reaches first --
lib/CompileJvm.gmk names itself for the same reason.

--- make/common/native/Link.gmk.orig
+++ make/common/native/Link.gmk
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@
           endif
         endif
         ifeq ($(OPENJDK_TARGET_OS_ENV), bsd.netbsd)
-          /usr/sbin/paxctl +m $$@
+	  /usr/sbin/paxctl +m $$@
         endif
         ifneq ($(MACOSX_CODESIGN_MODE), disabled)
           # Remove signature explicitly first to avoid warnings if the linker
